1
00:00:01,360 --> 00:00:02,960
So the module bundler

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:06,750
that we're gonna use in this course is called Parcel.

3
00:00:06,750 --> 00:00:09,560
And it's super fast and easy to use,

4
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:11,460
and, even more importantly,

5
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:15,410
it works out of the box without any configuration.

6
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:18,012
Now you might've heard of Webpack as well

7
00:00:18,012 --> 00:00:21,190
which is probably the most popular bundler

8
00:00:21,190 --> 00:00:24,140
and especially in react world.

9
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:28,510
However, it's way too complex to use in a course like this.

10
00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:31,083
And so let's now learn how to use Parcel.

11
00:00:32,950 --> 00:00:36,760
So Parcel is basically just another build tool

12
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:39,010
which is also on NPM.

13
00:00:39,010 --> 00:00:42,013
And so we will use NPM to install it.

14
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:46,540
So NPM install Parcel

15
00:00:46,540 --> 00:00:49,430
but this is now a different dependency.

16
00:00:49,430 --> 00:00:51,060
And so here we have to write

17
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:55,303
dash, dash, safe, dev like this.

18
00:00:56,360 --> 00:00:57,230
Okay?

19
00:00:57,230 --> 00:01:00,173
Then hit enter, and simply watch it install.

20
00:01:01,030 --> 00:01:04,480
So a devDependency is basically like a tool

21
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:07,650
that we need to build our application.

22
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:09,080
But it's not a dependency

23
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:12,030
that we actually include in our code.

24
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:12,863
All right.

25
00:01:12,863 --> 00:01:14,470
So it's simply a tool.

26
00:01:14,470 --> 00:01:17,980
And so that's why it's called a devDependency

27
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:22,770
because we can use it to develop our project.

28
00:01:22,770 --> 00:01:26,090
And so therefore it appears here in a new field,

29
00:01:26,090 --> 00:01:27,923
in our package.json file.

30
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:30,930
So again, these libraries,

31
00:01:30,930 --> 00:01:33,270
that we actually include in our code,

32
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:35,180
are the regular dependencies

33
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:39,550
and Parcel is a devDependency now, right?

34
00:01:39,550 --> 00:01:43,350
So let's clear the console here and actually use Parcel.

35
00:01:43,350 --> 00:01:45,270
So we do it here in the terminal

36
00:01:45,270 --> 00:01:47,290
because Parcel is basically

37
00:01:47,290 --> 00:01:50,380
just another command line interface.

38
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:54,393
However, we cannot simply run Parcel like this.

39
00:01:56,020 --> 00:01:58,270
So this is not going to work

40
00:01:58,270 --> 00:02:00,750
because the command is not found.

41
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:01,950
And the reason for that

42
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:04,280
is simply that this doesn't work

43
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:07,150
with locally installed packages.

44
00:02:07,150 --> 00:02:10,230
And Parcel was indeed installed locally.

45
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:12,660
So basically only on this project

46
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:16,040
and that's why it showed up in the package.json file

47
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:18,100
of this exact project.

48
00:02:18,100 --> 00:02:20,390
So there are also global installations

49
00:02:20,390 --> 00:02:23,700
but more about that by the end of this video.

50
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:26,640
Now, in order to still be able to use Parcel

51
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:30,100
here in the console, we have two options.

52
00:02:30,100 --> 00:02:32,560
So we can use something called NPX

53
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:35,900
or we can use NPM scripts.

54
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:37,970
So let's start with NPX,

55
00:02:37,970 --> 00:02:42,363
which is basically an application built into a NPM.

56
00:02:43,290 --> 00:02:45,200
So the details don't matter.

57
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:48,930
But what does matter is that we can simply use NPX

58
00:02:48,930 --> 00:02:53,351
to now run the same command as we did before,

59
00:02:53,351 --> 00:02:56,800
but this time it is going to work.

60
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:59,803
And so this is the normal command,

61
00:02:59,803 --> 00:03:02,800
and the option that we pass into Parcel

62
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:05,820
basically is this entry point.

63
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:08,830
So the entry point is index.html

64
00:03:08,830 --> 00:03:11,733
because that is where we include our script.js.

65
00:03:12,790 --> 00:03:16,110
So basically the file that we want to bundle up.

66
00:03:16,110 --> 00:03:20,290
So in our script.js, we are currently including

67
00:03:20,290 --> 00:03:23,713
this cloneDeep deep module from Lodash,

68
00:03:24,730 --> 00:03:26,874
and also let's actually put back

69
00:03:26,874 --> 00:03:29,570
this code from the beginning

70
00:03:29,570 --> 00:03:32,387
so that we are also importing

71
00:03:32,387 --> 00:03:35,610
our shoppingCart module from before.

72
00:03:35,610 --> 00:03:39,440
And so basically in this example, the goal of using Parcel

73
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:42,730
is to bundle these three modules together.

74
00:03:42,730 --> 00:03:47,730
So script.js together with shoppingCart.js

75
00:03:47,760 --> 00:03:50,753
and together with this cloneDeep.

76
00:03:52,250 --> 00:03:55,160
And so let's actually try this now.

77
00:03:55,160 --> 00:03:57,080
So I'm hitting enter here

78
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:58,890
and now it's going to take some time

79
00:03:58,890 --> 00:04:01,250
and do some magic behind the scenes,

80
00:04:01,250 --> 00:04:02,933
but now it is actually done.

81
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,872
So a Parcel actually then also starts

82
00:04:05,872 --> 00:04:08,893
a new development server on this URL.

83
00:04:10,090 --> 00:04:11,273
So let's click that.

84
00:04:12,410 --> 00:04:16,510
And so you'll see it opened a new tab right here.

85
00:04:16,510 --> 00:04:19,410
So basically besides only bundling,

86
00:04:19,410 --> 00:04:23,483
it also does exactly the same job as our live server.

87
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:27,370
So remember that we started this development server

88
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:30,830
using the live server package, right?

89
00:04:30,830 --> 00:04:33,500
And so this one here does exactly the same.

90
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:37,000
The difference is that this one is on port 8080,

91
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:40,130
and this one is on port 1234.

92
00:04:40,130 --> 00:04:42,330
And here we also have local hosts

93
00:04:42,330 --> 00:04:46,893
but that is exactly the same as the writing 127001.

94
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:50,360
So this is just the raw IP address

95
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:53,480
and local host is the nicer name.

96
00:04:53,480 --> 00:04:54,760
All right.

97
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:58,400
Now, if you did have any errors by doing this,

98
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:01,020
so maybe you couldn't even install Parcel,

99
00:05:01,020 --> 00:05:02,770
or maybe you got some error

100
00:05:02,770 --> 00:05:05,530
while you were trying to run this command

101
00:05:05,530 --> 00:05:08,563
then let me help you troubleshoot that.

102
00:05:10,070 --> 00:05:13,190
So to do that, I'm going to open a new terminal here

103
00:05:13,190 --> 00:05:16,020
and we can do that by clicking this plus.

104
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:17,313
And so now we have three.

105
00:05:18,410 --> 00:05:21,530
And this first one we actually don't need anymore.

106
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:24,630
So this one is still running our live server.

107
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:29,630
And so let's canceled that by hitting control, C, okay?

108
00:05:29,670 --> 00:05:33,900
And again, that's because Parcel already does that same job.

109
00:05:33,900 --> 00:05:37,100
And so right now we no longer need this

110
00:05:37,100 --> 00:05:41,000
and so now it's not working anymore, so let's close it.

111
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:43,700
And the same for this terminal window.

112
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:47,497
But anyway, let's go back to the one we were using.

113
00:05:47,497 --> 00:05:50,810
And so again, if you had any error installing it,

114
00:05:50,810 --> 00:05:53,410
you can try installing it with sudo

115
00:05:53,410 --> 00:05:56,560
which will give you basically more permissions.

116
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:57,980
So you write sudo,

117
00:05:57,980 --> 00:06:00,850
and then exactly the same command as before.

118
00:06:00,850 --> 00:06:04,040
So NPM install Parcel.

119
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:06,370
This will then ask you for your password

120
00:06:06,370 --> 00:06:09,200
and then hopefully that's going to work.

121
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:11,000
Now, if that doesn't fix it,

122
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,950
then you have to install exactly the same version

123
00:06:13,950 --> 00:06:15,433
as I am using here.

124
00:06:16,350 --> 00:06:20,080
So we can read that in our package.json file.

125
00:06:20,080 --> 00:06:24,363
And so here you see that I'm using version 1.12.4.

126
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:29,930
And so you can NPM install exactly this version

127
00:06:29,930 --> 00:06:34,930
by writing at and then 1.12.4.

128
00:06:35,150 --> 00:06:38,060
So maybe you have version two already installed

129
00:06:38,060 --> 00:06:41,000
because it's going to be coming out very soon

130
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:43,250
and then that might break something.

131
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:46,210
And so therefore it's best to use this version,

132
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:50,220
1.12.4, at least in this project.

133
00:06:50,220 --> 00:06:54,040
In the next project, we will probably use version two.

134
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:55,950
And if that still doesn't fix it,

135
00:06:55,950 --> 00:06:58,130
then before doing this command,

136
00:06:58,130 --> 00:07:00,630
you can try to uninstall it first.

137
00:07:00,630 --> 00:07:05,630
So NPM uninstall Parcel like this.

138
00:07:06,290 --> 00:07:07,810
And then after that,

139
00:07:07,810 --> 00:07:10,550
you can try again to install this version.

140
00:07:10,550 --> 00:07:13,240
And so then you should be good to go.

141
00:07:13,240 --> 00:07:15,323
So you should have no more errors then.

142
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:18,100
Okay.

143
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:19,390
Now speaking of errors,

144
00:07:19,390 --> 00:07:23,380
we do actually have one error here coming from our code.

145
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:25,560
But the problem for all of that

146
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:28,923
is that we still have this type module here.

147
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:31,930
However, what Parcel does

148
00:07:31,930 --> 00:07:35,420
is that it basically, simply, creates a script.

149
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:39,090
And so now we are actually no longer using a module

150
00:07:39,090 --> 00:07:42,450
but we are back to using a regular script.

151
00:07:42,450 --> 00:07:43,550
And that is important

152
00:07:43,550 --> 00:07:47,100
because modules do not work in older browsers.

153
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:52,100
So let's comment this one out just so we can also keep it.

154
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:56,620
Then I'm deleting this part and then let's give it a save

155
00:07:56,620 --> 00:08:00,940
so that Parcel can rebuild this application.

156
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:03,053
And great, the error is gone.

157
00:08:04,182 --> 00:08:05,015
Okay.

158
00:08:05,015 --> 00:08:09,320
But now let's actually take a look at what Parcel did here.

159
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:13,270
So what it did was to create this dist folder,

160
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:15,390
which stands for distribution,

161
00:08:15,390 --> 00:08:18,360
because it is essentially gonna be this folder

162
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,780
that we will send for production.

163
00:08:20,780 --> 00:08:23,160
So basically it's the code in this folder

164
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:26,260
that we will send to our final users.

165
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:29,760
So you'll see it created a new index.html here

166
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:32,703
and also a bunch of JavaScript files.

167
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:37,110
So let's take a look at this index here.

168
00:08:37,110 --> 00:08:40,140
And so you see that indeed it is a new one

169
00:08:40,140 --> 00:08:42,070
because the included script here

170
00:08:42,070 --> 00:08:45,500
is now no longer the one that we built ourselves

171
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:50,500
but it is script, dot and then all of this here.

172
00:08:52,500 --> 00:08:57,500
And so this new script here is basically the bundle itself.

173
00:08:57,680 --> 00:09:01,233
So it's this file, and so let's analyze it here as well.

174
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:03,680
Okay.

175
00:09:03,680 --> 00:09:06,090
And so here you already see that it does include

176
00:09:06,090 --> 00:09:10,650
some of the stuff that we have in our other modules.

177
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:15,063
So importing module, for example, we had in script.js.

178
00:09:17,190 --> 00:09:18,863
Let's see what else we have here.

179
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:22,290
So here you see a bunch of stuff

180
00:09:22,290 --> 00:09:25,223
that is created by Parcel, of course.

181
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:30,760
So this is basically the cloneDeep function,

182
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,653
probably, at some point here.

183
00:09:34,510 --> 00:09:37,893
So you see a lot of code created by Parcel.

184
00:09:40,470 --> 00:09:42,880
But, yeah.

185
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:45,690
So in the real world, you will not take a look at this code,

186
00:09:45,690 --> 00:09:47,310
but I just wanted to show you

187
00:09:47,310 --> 00:09:50,710
that, of course, all of our code is now in here.

188
00:09:50,710 --> 00:09:54,320
So let's just search for cloneDeep, for example.

189
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,543
So the one that we used.

190
00:09:56,840 --> 00:10:01,330
And so it's gotta be somewhere down here as a function.

191
00:10:01,330 --> 00:10:04,100
And so indeed all the code that we had before,

192
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:08,733
spread across multiple modules, is now all in this script.

193
00:10:09,850 --> 00:10:12,427
And so that's exactly the goal that we had.

194
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:18,220
And unused code has probably also not yet been removed

195
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:20,670
but we will leave that for later.

196
00:10:20,670 --> 00:10:23,180
So that's going to be the build step

197
00:10:23,180 --> 00:10:26,620
but what we're doing right now is the development step.

198
00:10:26,620 --> 00:10:28,270
And so in order for us to be able

199
00:10:28,270 --> 00:10:31,130
to check the code during development,

200
00:10:31,130 --> 00:10:33,003
it will not compress everything.

201
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:36,853
All right?

202
00:10:36,853 --> 00:10:41,853
So we can close all of this and go back to our script here

203
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:43,890
because I want to show you something.

204
00:10:45,090 --> 00:10:49,070
So of course, whenever we now save this file,

205
00:10:49,070 --> 00:10:51,420
then it will reload this file here,

206
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:55,950
just as we had before with live server, right?

207
00:10:55,950 --> 00:11:00,587
So as I saved you see that everything here reloaded, right?

208
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:04,100
And we can see that here as well.

209
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:06,750
So take a look at what happens when I save this here.

210
00:11:07,670 --> 00:11:10,630
Then you'll see this happened again.

211
00:11:10,630 --> 00:11:14,580
However, in Parcel, we can activate something even better,

212
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:17,930
which is called hot module replacement.

213
00:11:17,930 --> 00:11:22,930
So we can write if module.hot, like this,

214
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:29,147
then module.hot.accept.

215
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:36,770
Now this code here is code that only Parcel understands.

216
00:11:36,770 --> 00:11:40,280
And so of course it will not make it into our final bundle

217
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:43,313
because the browser is not going to understand any of it.

218
00:11:44,220 --> 00:11:47,310
But anyway, what hot module reloading means

219
00:11:47,310 --> 00:11:50,320
is that whenever we change one of the modules,

220
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:54,020
it will then, of course, trigger a rebuild, like this,

221
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:58,250
but that new modified bundle will then automatically,

222
00:11:58,250 --> 00:12:01,650
like magic, get injected into the browser

223
00:12:01,650 --> 00:12:04,860
without triggering a whole page reload.

224
00:12:04,860 --> 00:12:06,220
All right.

225
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:08,570
So again, whenever we change something here,

226
00:12:08,570 --> 00:12:11,960
this will then not reload this part of the page.

227
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,600
And so that's going to be amazing

228
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:16,350
for maintaining state on our page

229
00:12:16,350 --> 00:12:18,660
whenever we are testing out something.

230
00:12:18,660 --> 00:12:21,610
So this used to be something quite annoying in the past.

231
00:12:21,610 --> 00:12:24,020
For example, in our Bankist the application,

232
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:26,400
where whenever we reloaded the page,

233
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:29,530
we needed to log in again into the application.

234
00:12:29,530 --> 00:12:30,850
Remember that?

235
00:12:30,850 --> 00:12:33,720
But with Parcel and hot module replacement,

236
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:35,490
that's not going to happen,

237
00:12:35,490 --> 00:12:38,300
because the page will not reload.

238
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:39,380
So if I save this now,

239
00:12:39,380 --> 00:12:42,300
then probably it's going to look the same.

240
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:45,160
But again, if we had some state here on the page,

241
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:46,873
then that would be maintained.

242
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:51,603
Okay, next up, let's change something here.

243
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:57,860
So as I said, when we first included this cloneDeep here,

244
00:12:58,370 --> 00:13:03,370
from lodash, this is quite cumbersome doing it like this.

245
00:13:03,394 --> 00:13:05,790
And so that's why in all module bundlers,

246
00:13:05,790 --> 00:13:07,630
there's no need for specifying

247
00:13:07,630 --> 00:13:10,650
the entire path to any module.

248
00:13:10,650 --> 00:13:12,703
So instead we can simply do this.

249
00:13:13,890 --> 00:13:17,090
So keeping this here just for reference,

250
00:13:17,090 --> 00:13:18,840
and then all we need to say

251
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:22,733
is that we want to include the lodash library.

252
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:26,240
And so Parcel will then automatically

253
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:29,060
find the path to this module,

254
00:13:29,060 --> 00:13:31,720
and will simply import it like this

255
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:34,230
without us having to manually tie up

256
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,893
the entire path to there.

257
00:13:36,810 --> 00:13:41,130
And so that's a lot more useful than what we had before.

258
00:13:41,130 --> 00:13:44,420
And in fact, this works with all kinds of assets.

259
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:49,220
So even with HTML or CSS or SAS files,

260
00:13:49,220 --> 00:13:53,870
or even images, and of course also all kinds of modules.

261
00:13:53,870 --> 00:13:56,200
So not only ESX modules,

262
00:13:56,200 --> 00:14:00,200
but this is also going to work with CommonJS modules.

263
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:02,360
So let me actually show that to you.

264
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:06,630
So instead of importing a DES version of lodash,

265
00:14:06,630 --> 00:14:09,393
we can simply import lodash like this.

266
00:14:10,490 --> 00:14:12,743
So just a regular version of lodash

267
00:14:13,730 --> 00:14:15,920
and Parcel is even smart enough

268
00:14:15,920 --> 00:14:18,663
to then automatically install this package here.

269
00:14:21,950 --> 00:14:23,110
Okay.

270
00:14:23,110 --> 00:14:27,853
So now if we go to our package.json right here,

271
00:14:29,290 --> 00:14:31,550
well, it's probably not here.

272
00:14:31,550 --> 00:14:34,500
So it looks like maybe it didn't install it.

273
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:37,583
So probably it's simply still using this one.

274
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:40,083
Okay.

275
00:14:40,083 --> 00:14:43,740
But anyway, what I said is still true.

276
00:14:43,740 --> 00:14:45,890
So Parcel can indeed work

277
00:14:45,890 --> 00:14:48,820
with all the CommonJS modules as well.

278
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:51,290
And so this way we can then simply use

279
00:14:51,290 --> 00:14:54,520
all the modules that are available on NPM

280
00:14:54,520 --> 00:14:58,020
and which still use this older module format.

281
00:14:58,020 --> 00:15:01,630
So let's leave it like this, save it again.

282
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:05,640
And maybe you have been noticing that this cart right here

283
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:08,690
keeps growing and growing and growing.

284
00:15:08,690 --> 00:15:10,496
So if we take a look at this,

285
00:15:10,496 --> 00:15:14,770
you see that we are adding these three products

286
00:15:14,770 --> 00:15:16,690
over and over again.

287
00:15:16,690 --> 00:15:21,030
And so the reason for that is hot module replacement.

288
00:15:21,030 --> 00:15:25,130
So the state is maintained whenever we reload the page here.

289
00:15:25,130 --> 00:15:27,903
And so that's exactly what we can now observe here.

290
00:15:29,490 --> 00:15:30,400
Okay.

291
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:32,910
So if we save it again, then we will have 15

292
00:15:34,040 --> 00:15:37,830
because we are simply adding new objects into this object

293
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:42,830
that keeps persisting over page reloads, basically.

294
00:15:43,130 --> 00:15:45,450
And so this works with all state,

295
00:15:45,450 --> 00:15:48,930
and again, it's going to be really, really helpful.

296
00:15:48,930 --> 00:15:49,780
Okay.

297
00:15:49,780 --> 00:15:54,490
So this is how Parcel works and let me know, finish it here

298
00:15:54,490 --> 00:15:58,020
because remember the way we executed Parcel first

299
00:15:58,020 --> 00:16:03,020
was by saying a NPX Parcel and then index.html.

300
00:16:04,110 --> 00:16:06,710
However, I mentioned that there is a second way,

301
00:16:06,710 --> 00:16:09,360
which is to use NPM script.

302
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:13,070
And so that's the way we actually use it in practice.

303
00:16:13,070 --> 00:16:16,370
So NPM scripts are basically another way

304
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:21,773
of running a locally installed packages in the command line.

305
00:16:23,350 --> 00:16:27,910
They also allow us to basically automate repetitive tasks.

306
00:16:27,910 --> 00:16:31,690
And so therefore we then don't have to write NPX Parcel

307
00:16:31,690 --> 00:16:34,773
and all of that, every time that we want to use it.

308
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:38,067
So we can simply create a script here,

309
00:16:38,067 --> 00:16:40,363
and let me delete this one here,

310
00:16:41,530 --> 00:16:44,073
let me just delete all of it and create a new one.

311
00:16:45,700 --> 00:16:49,420
So we need to double quote and then the name of the script

312
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:51,793
and the default is start here,

313
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:57,330
and then here comes the script itself.

314
00:16:57,330 --> 00:16:58,620
And so the script is going to

315
00:16:58,620 --> 00:17:03,620
be simply Parcel index.html.

316
00:17:04,610 --> 00:17:07,330
So again, we can't write this command

317
00:17:07,330 --> 00:17:09,570
directly in the command line,

318
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:13,190
but we can write it in the NPM script.

319
00:17:13,190 --> 00:17:15,900
And so let's now go back to our console

320
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:20,040
and try it out and actually run this command.

321
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:24,120
NPM run and then start.

322
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:27,140
And so start is the name of the NPM script

323
00:17:27,140 --> 00:17:28,333
that we defined here.

324
00:17:30,150 --> 00:17:31,590
So let's try that.

325
00:17:31,590 --> 00:17:32,763
And here we go.

326
00:17:34,770 --> 00:17:36,960
So it's doing the same thing as before

327
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,593
but now we have the simple command

328
00:17:38,593 --> 00:17:42,630
that we can execute whenever we want to start Parcel

329
00:17:42,630 --> 00:17:46,500
and whenever we want to start developing, basically.

330
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:47,380
All right.

331
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:51,453
And so again, that is mainly how we do it in development.

332
00:17:53,290 --> 00:17:54,530
Okay.

333
00:17:54,530 --> 00:17:56,620
And speaking of development,

334
00:17:56,620 --> 00:17:59,480
whenever we are done developing our project,

335
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:02,670
it is time to build the final bundle.

336
00:18:02,670 --> 00:18:04,680
So the bundle that is compressed

337
00:18:04,680 --> 00:18:08,560
and has dead code elimination and all of that.

338
00:18:08,560 --> 00:18:11,920
And so for that, we need another Parcel command.

339
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:15,350
And so let's add that as another script here.

340
00:18:15,350 --> 00:18:16,570
So we need to come up

341
00:18:16,570 --> 00:18:19,943
and then this one will be called build.

342
00:18:22,320 --> 00:18:27,320
And so Parcel, build, and then again, index.html.

343
00:18:30,880 --> 00:18:33,453
So let's stop this one here actually,

344
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:39,843
and now let's run NPM run build.

345
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,740
So this might take some more time this time

346
00:18:45,610 --> 00:18:48,550
because it's doing a lot more work behind the scenes,

347
00:18:48,550 --> 00:18:50,143
but let's just wait for it.

348
00:18:52,320 --> 00:18:53,260
All right.

349
00:18:53,260 --> 00:18:55,950
And so now we even get this nice output

350
00:18:55,950 --> 00:18:57,623
with the sizes of everything.

351
00:18:58,580 --> 00:19:01,713
And so let's now take a look at our dist folder,

352
00:19:03,050 --> 00:19:04,170
and you see immediately

353
00:19:04,170 --> 00:19:07,640
that this HTML looks different, right?

354
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:09,910
It is compressed now.

355
00:19:09,910 --> 00:19:12,850
So the script that we can then ship to the browser

356
00:19:12,850 --> 00:19:15,870
and ship to our users is this one.

357
00:19:15,870 --> 00:19:18,523
So ending in FD3.

358
00:19:19,730 --> 00:19:23,070
So this one, all right.

359
00:19:23,070 --> 00:19:26,910
And again, you see that it looks quite different.

360
00:19:26,910 --> 00:19:30,283
Everything is compressed into this unreadable mess,

361
00:19:31,160 --> 00:19:34,210
but it is, of course, a lot more performance

362
00:19:34,210 --> 00:19:36,590
than the script that we had before.

363
00:19:36,590 --> 00:19:39,343
And so that's why Parcel does this for us.

364
00:19:40,230 --> 00:19:41,700
And we will, again, come back

365
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:44,230
to all of this in the real world

366
00:19:44,230 --> 00:19:48,410
once we actually move to our next more real project

367
00:19:48,410 --> 00:19:50,703
in which we're going to use all of this.

368
00:19:52,170 --> 00:19:53,940
Now, just to finish this lecture,

369
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:55,310
I also wanted to mention

370
00:19:55,310 --> 00:19:59,200
that we can also install packages globally.

371
00:19:59,200 --> 00:20:01,510
And so that would work like this.

372
00:20:01,510 --> 00:20:06,510
So NPM install Parcel, and then G which stands for global.

373
00:20:08,660 --> 00:20:09,960
And this is actually the way

374
00:20:09,960 --> 00:20:13,060
that we installed the live server package before.

375
00:20:13,060 --> 00:20:14,300
And so, because of that,

376
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:17,430
we were then simply able to use live server

377
00:20:17,430 --> 00:20:20,350
in every directory on our computer.

378
00:20:20,350 --> 00:20:22,310
So basically the big difference

379
00:20:22,310 --> 00:20:26,130
between globally and locally installed packages

380
00:20:26,130 --> 00:20:29,980
and especially these tools like Parcel or live server,

381
00:20:29,980 --> 00:20:31,840
is that we can use the global tools

382
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:33,760
directly in the command line

383
00:20:33,760 --> 00:20:37,840
without the intermediate step of an NPM script.

384
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:41,580
However, most of these tools actually advise developers

385
00:20:41,580 --> 00:20:44,950
to always install the tools locally

386
00:20:44,950 --> 00:20:48,210
so that they can always stay on the latest version.

387
00:20:48,210 --> 00:20:51,280
And so usually I follow that approach as well.

388
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:55,477
And so I'm not going to install Parcel globally like this.

389
00:20:55,477 --> 00:20:57,050
Okay.

390
00:20:57,050 --> 00:21:00,830
And that's the fundamentals of bundling with Parcel

391
00:21:00,830 --> 00:21:04,400
and of using build tools with NPM.

392
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:07,730
So I introduced a lot of different concepts here.

393
00:21:07,730 --> 00:21:10,560
So to make sure to review this,

394
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:13,880
especially this part about the NPM scripts,

395
00:21:13,880 --> 00:21:16,330
maybe that might be confusing

396
00:21:16,330 --> 00:21:19,030
and also take a look at the output files

397
00:21:19,030 --> 00:21:21,170
that Parcel gives us.

398
00:21:21,170 --> 00:21:23,570
So just take some time to review

399
00:21:23,570 --> 00:21:25,410
all that we did in this video.

400
00:21:25,410 --> 00:21:29,446
And if after that, this is all still very confusing to you,

401
00:21:29,446 --> 00:21:31,210
then don't worry.

402
00:21:31,210 --> 00:21:33,700
I'm sure that it will make total sense

403
00:21:33,700 --> 00:21:37,243
once we actually use this in our next big project.